+-- HA-DEGRADED-READ-1 (2026-10-19, pillar reach; agent_issues 2040, 2945 and 2607, qnfo-fleet-dashboard 1.52.0).
+-- APPLY-BY: ci
+-- DB: qnfo-audit
+-- Rollback: UPDATE remediation_contracts SET verify_probe = (SELECT b.verify_probe FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), status = (SELECT b.status FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), expected_cadence_h = (SELECT b.expected_cadence_h FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), attempts = (SELECT b.attempts FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), last_verdict = (SELECT b.last_verdict FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class), next_due_at = (SELECT b.next_due_at FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts b WHERE b.class = remediation_contracts.class) WHERE class IN (SELECT class FROM bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts); DELETE FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class = 'fm-rum-degraded-read'; DELETE FROM failure_modes WHERE fm_key = 'rum-degraded-read'; DELETE FROM control_registry WHERE control = 'rum-degraded-read-guard'
+-- spof-review: adds none (the guard reads the ledger it writes and fails open to the old publish when that ledger is unreadable); removes the single unguarded read that two metrics and two issues depended on.
+--
+-- WHAT WAS WRONG (read from qnfo-audit 2026-10-19, after the 12:31Z run)
+-- qnfo-fleet-dashboard refreshHumanAudience rejected only an error or a group-limit hit, then wrote metric_registry and reach_signals for
+-- any group list, and refreshRegistryMetrics summed whatever groups came back. A Web Analytics read that SUCCEEDS with a fraction of the
+-- data therefore became a published number, twice on the same day:
+--   - 10:31Z: the human-audience ledger row said external 0 with 7 rows (the days before hold 23 to 24 rows: cloud_ops_events
+--     human-audience-2026-10-15..18 carry rows 23, 23, 24, 24); the next run replaced that row (the day id is INSERT OR REPLACE), so the
+--     10:31Z values are the session's own read from that hour, and metric_history holds external 210 and growth +128.90 at 12:00Z on
+--     10-19, so the registry was good again before 12:31Z;
+--   - 12:31Z: it happened again and the row is still there: human-audience-2026-10-19 ts 12:31:26.571Z meta {external 0, continuation 2000,
+--     direct 4000, rows 5} with no guard key; metric_registry external_referred_pageviews_7d reads '0' (refreshed 12:31:26Z) and
+--     continuation_pageviews_7d '2000', while pageviews_30d (12020), impressions_growth_30d (+127.65%) and referral_30d (620) refreshed
+--     at 12:31:09Z in the same hour, so the 7-day audience query alone returned the partial list; v_metric_trigger_state id 1820
+--     (external_referred_pageviews_7d under 50) has hit 1 now;
+--   - agent_issues 2945 was filed on impressions_growth_30d = -100, which is what an empty current window gives (pv30 0 against a
+--     prior window), and the same hour wrote "n/a: prior window has 7 of 30 days" over a good figure;
+--   - each swing reopened a METRIC-TRIGGER issue (1820, 370) that recovered an hour later when the same query returned the full list:
+--     metric_history shows external 240 and 210 on 10-18 and 10-19 and growth +134.41 and +128.90, and the target is not wrong. The file's
+--     own comment says a failed read must leave rows untouched; a partial read was the case it did not cover.
+-- The audience ledger since 2026-10-08 (rows per day: 56, 45, 42, 16, 18, 19, 19, 23, 23, 24, 24) is the evidence for the thresholds.
+--
+-- WHAT THIS CHANGES
+--   worker (1.52.0)   refreshHumanAudience compares each read with a baseline and writes nothing on a hit. The baseline is the newest
+--                     human-audience row that PASSED the guard (meta.guard ok, no note saying it was accepted unchecked or past its
+--                     expiry) among the last seven; a row of the pre-1.52.0 code, such as the 12:31Z one, never sets the bar, and with
+--                     no passed row the baseline is the row with the most groups. A hit is: rows under half of the baseline count
+--                     (baseline at least 10) AND page loads under 80 percent of the baseline, or external fallen to 0, or external
+--                     under half of a baseline external of 50 or more; or page loads under half; or external 0 after 50 or more with
+--                     rows under 75 percent. refreshRegistryMetrics holds pageviews_30d and referral_30d when the window is empty or
+--                     under HALF of the stored value (the first round's 30 percent floor published both real partial referral reads,
+--                     620 -> 200 on 2026-10-18 12:30Z and 2026-10-19 06:31Z, which are 32.3 percent), pageviews_30d also when it is
+--                     more than 125 percent of a stored value of 1000 or more (10540 -> 16000 at 13:31Z and 11330 -> 16000 at 16:31Z on
+--                     10-18, each back within the hour; the 44 logged hourly writes of pageviews_30d moved by at most +4.9 and -3.7 percent
+--                     when they were real), and impressions_growth_30d when the current window is empty or the prior window covers fewer
+--                     days than the stored figure rested on. referral_30d has no ceiling: no upward spike is logged for it. Every
+--                     human-audience ledger row carries meta.guard; a hold writes a human-audience-degraded (or registry-rum-degraded)
+--                     ledger row instead.
+--   expiry            no hold without one (ANTIFRAGILE-1, QUEUE-SLA-1): a hold lasts one read, the next read is accepted whatever it
+--                     says, so a held figure is never more than about 120 minutes old; an accepted read that agrees with the held one
+--                     (within a factor of two) becomes a baseline, one that does not is marked "hold expired" and does not; no
+--                     baseline means no hold; an unreadable or unwritable ledger fails open to the old publish. impressions_growth_30d
+--                     rests on both windows, so a hold of the current window or of the prior window counts against its one read: it is
+--                     never held twice in a row (two different degradations on consecutive reads kept it for 180 minutes in round 1).
+--   control_registry  rum-degraded-read-guard (kind guard, disposition keep, removal condition in its evidence).
+--   failure_modes     rum-degraded-read with the detector fm-rum-degraded-read: the newest human-audience or human-audience-degraded
+--                     ledger row is at most 6 hours old and carries meta.guard. It fails until the 1.52.0 refresh has run once, and a
+--                     held read (which writes only a degraded row) clears it like an accepted one.
+--   contracts         the closing probe belongs to the issue that is OPEN when the migration applies: METRIC-TRIGGER-1820 is issue 2607
+--                     (open, updated 13:01Z; its contract issue-2607 is superseded 'contract-on-closed-issue' from before it was
+--                     reopened), not the closed issue 2040. Its contract is re-armed active with a probe that reads 'pending: guard marker
+--                     not live yet' while the newest ledger row has no guard marker, and 'pending: the guard is holding a degraded read'
+--                     while the trigger is in breach and the newest ledger row is a held read (the poisoned value is replaced by the next
+--                     read, so a held first read can never count as a failure), and afterwards the metric, three days of reach_signals
+--                     at 50 or more; it reads 1 only after the guarded refresh ran and the metric recovered, and 0 for a real breach. The
+--                     contracts of the closed issues 2040 and 2945 are NOT touched: re-arming a closed issue's contract reopens a
+--                     duplicate of the open one after three failed probes, and a monitoring contract (issue-2945) is never probed at
+--                     all, because the remediation tick and scripts/remediation_consumer.py select only active and holding contracts, so
+--                     a probe written there would claim a check that never runs. The superseded probe of the contract that is re-armed
+--                     is kept in bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts, which the Rollback line restores; when no issue is open for the
+--                     trigger the table is empty and nothing is armed. The standing detector fm-rum-degraded-read is never parked
+--                     (DETECTOR-NEVER-PARKS-2) and is the durable check; red-drain may park the re-armed contract as monitoring
+--                     (TRIGGER-RECOVERY-1 closes those), which is fine because the detector stays.
+--   decision_log      appended (append-only: the Rollback line does not touch it).
+-- Verified against live D1 before writing (read-only, 2026-10-19 after 12:31Z): the human-audience ledger rows 10-08 to 10-19 and their
+-- metas as quoted above; metric_registry values and refresh times as quoted; v_metric_trigger_state ids 369 (referral_30d, hit 0),
+-- 370 (impressions_growth_30d, 127.65, hit 0) and 1820 (external_referred_pageviews_7d, 0, hit 1); cloud_ops_events.meta is JSON text; ts
+-- is ISO with T and Z, so the detector compares against strftime with the same shape (a datetime() bound sorts below every T timestamp
+-- of the same day).
+
+CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bak_20261019_rum_guard_contracts AS
+  SELECT * FROM remediation_contracts WHERE class IN (SELECT 'issue-' || id FROM agent_issues WHERE status = 'open' AND title LIKE 'METRIC-TRIGGER-1820-%');
+
+INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_registry (control, location, kind, guards_against, critical_path, disposition, disposition_state, alternate_path, alternate_tested_at, evidence, issue_id) VALUES
+ ('rum-degraded-read-guard',
+  'qnfo-fleet-dashboard worker.js humanAudienceGuard, humanAudienceBaseline and humanAudienceGuardCheck (refreshHumanAudience), rumRegistryGuardCheck (refreshRegistryMetrics), HA-DEGRADED-READ-1',
