+  0, 'keep', 'applied',
+  'the hold expires by itself: it lasts one read and the next read is accepted whatever it says, so a held figure is never more than about 120 minutes old (QUEUE-SLA-1); a ledger that cannot be read or written fails open to the pre-guard publish. human-audience.test.mjs sections 6e to 6q and 7e to 7t run each path',
+  '2026-10-19',
+  'REASON: a degraded read must not write a number. MEASURED 2026-10-19: the audience read returned 7 groups against 24 at 10:31Z and 5 groups at 12:31Z and both were published as external 0 (ledger row human-audience-2026-10-19 ts 12:31:26Z: rows 5, external 0, continuation 2000, direct 4000, no guard key; trigger 1820 hit 1); impressions growth was filed at -100 (agent_issues 2945) from an empty current window. EXPIRY / REMOVAL CONDITION: remove when the read is checked against two consecutive reads at the source (a double read would make this comparison redundant); until then the hold lasts one read. COST: a genuine collapse is published one hourly read late, and a held read shows as a metric_staleness_breaches row when the next accepted read lands. THRESHOLDS are constants in worker.js (RUM_GUARD_*), chosen from the live series (rows 16 to 56 and external 105 to 390 between 2026-10-08 and 10-18). The one large step in it, 10-10 to 10-11 (42 groups to 16 while page loads rose from 1295 to 1490 and external from 115 to 200), is a real change, so rows under half of the baseline count only with page loads under 80 percent of it, external falling to 0 or external under half of the baseline; the registry floor is half of the stored value because the real partial referral reads were 32 percent of it, and pageviews_30d has a ceiling of 125 percent for the 16000 reads of 10-18; the audience test replays the 13 real daily rows of 2026-10-06 to 10-18 and holds none of them. The baseline is the newest row that passed the guard because a pre-guard row can itself be a partial read (the 12:31Z one is).',
