x, read a message in full; owner session), service bindings to qnfo-email, qnfo-cloud-ops and qnfo-fleet-control for call, and sql reads of q08 and the private identity D1 (owner session; identity stays read-only). info shows the signed-in owner up to 1500 characters of each message and tells a visitor to sign in for subject and text. MAIL-ASK-1 (same day, owner: "what do they say? don't waste my time"): "WHAT'S UP WITH RESEARCHLETTERS EMAILS?" and the follow-up "AND WHAT DO THEY SAY?" reached the model with no message at all (MAIL_ASK_RX had no plurals, "researchletters" did not name theresearchletters.org, a follow-up named no sender); plurals, say/said/content, a card domain typed without "the" or the TLD, and a follow-up with mail cards in the queue now read the messages, and the owner's context carries 1500 characters of each (was 300). A journal call for papers ("We invite your research article", "submit your full-length article", "fits our journal scope", an ISSN line) is a solicitation, not a person owed a reply (MAIL_SOLICIT_RX, parity with qnfo-cloud-ops 1.25.2), so it leaves the owner queue and is listed as handled. INBOX-REPLY-1 (same day, owner: "THE FLEET DASHBOARD IS THE QNFO INBOX"): inbox cards carry Reply (fills "reply <id> " in the command line), Read and Spam; "reply <id> <text>" sends through qnfo-email /send as the address the mail was written to (rowan.quni@qnfo.org by default) with "Re: <subject>", marks the message replied and closes its queue rows (fresh code: it speaks in the owner's name); "spam <id> ..." marks messages spam and adds the sender to email_sender_policy junk; the card no longer says "Open the qnfo inbox". */ /* 1.30.1: hosts fold to their property by domain, probe clicks left out, 64-character campaign tags matched, ingest notes carry no upstream error text. 1.30.0 FLEET-KPI-1 (owner request 2026-10-12, pillar reach): a Metrics tab (/kpi, JSON /api/kpi, open to everyone) computed from qnfo-audit at request time: open issues by priority and category, opened and closed per day, median age, oldest, closed with evidence in 24 h and 7 d, code-loop tasks; bot-filtered page views per property and day, outreach actions and events per channel and day, posts per channel, the most popular posts with links, subscribers, mentions and citations; the Buffer channels, posts and per-post statistics; a value nothing measures is null and shown as not measured; the daily reach ingest adds a per-host row with page loads and visits. */ /* 1.29.4 CMD-AI-TIMEOUT-1 (agent_issues 2316): cmdModelCall sends timeout_ms just under its own abort and names a 504 router_timeout; WATCHMAKER-TICK-LEDGER-1 (2363): tick-sequence-ledger entry, duplicate dangling-bindings-census entry removed; REPORT-CARD-CATCHUP-1 (2054): the weekly card is caught up on any tick and deduped only against measured rows. */ /* 1.29.3 WORKERS-BEST-PRACTICES-1: every LOOP_TOKEN check (6 POST routes + the machine flag) uses constEq instead of !==/===. */ /* 1.29.2 MODEL-ID-AUDIT-1 (2026-10-11): qnfo-ai routes only the ids in its MODELS table; llama-3.3-70b-instruct-fp8-fast is not one, so the third ask leg silently became a second deepseek-v4-flash. Order is now glm-5.3-flash, deepseek-v4-flash-wa, gpt-oss-120b: the Workers AI legs probe at 2-3 s through qnfo-ai, the DeepSeek API leg at 13 s. */ /* 1.29.1 CMD-ASK-BUDGET-1 (2026-10-11): 1.29.0 raised CMD_AI_BUDGET_MS to 40 s, but the job runs in ctx.waitUntil, which the runtime cancels 30 s after the response, so the first live ask (cmd-517f7562d37f1041ef0a) never wrote its fallback and stayed running until the page gave up at 45 s; the budget is back under that limit (24 s, hedge 4 s) and a suite asserts it stays below 28 s. 1.29.0 CMD-ASK-FAST-1 (2026-10-11, pillar autonomy; owner: "Fix fleet command line"): every command-line and Ask question since 2026-10-06 ended in the stored-data fallback ("The AI model did not answer just now (it timed out)", 7 of the last 7 rows): ASK_MODELS named glm-5.2, a model qnfo-ai no longer lists, so the first call burned its slot and glm-5.3-flash, asked second with the remaining budget, timed out at 13 s. The models are now raced with a staggered start (ASK_HEDGE_MS, first answer wins; each failure names its model in cmd_log.error), the budget is 40 s, and a question about Q08 reads published_pieces from the q08-signal D1 (new read binding Q08) into the model context and into the no-model fallback, which also says plainly when its stored data does not cover the question instead of answering with a status dump. 1.28.2 1.28.2 NOZ-DOI-1 (2026-10-10, pillar reach): no deposit-service (10.5281) data is collected, scored or shown: reach rows, the impact KPI, the identity-weekly lookups and the watchmaker op are removed, and entity_map ignores that DOI prefix. 1.28.1 NO-MEMORY-FACTS-1 (owner directive 2026-10-10): the public Ask and command prompts state that no fact, name, figure or history may come from outside CONTEXT. */ /* 1.28.0 CONSOLE-BUDGET-WRITE-1 (agent_issues 2072, 2026-10-08, pillar autonomy): the console accepts sql! writes to fleet_budget (RULE-8-RETIRED-1: the fleet sets its own spend limits), with the same WHERE, row cap, console_backups copy and confirm button as every other write. 1.27.0 DASHBOARD-AUTONOMY-FIRST-1 (2026-10-08, agent_issues 2171, pillars autonomy and research): SCALE_BACK no longer puts "Decide: scale the fleet back" in the owner queue (spend caps are the fleet's, charter rules 10 and 11; /api/human carries spend_decision "fleet"), and a question about research, the pipeline, papers or the queue reads research_queue facts into Ask and its no-model fallback; the 15-minute cron is the second direct producer of qnfo-audit.fleet_tick (D1-TRIGGER-DEPTH-1). 1.26.8 (2026-10-08, pillar autonomy, PROBE-RUNNER-WATCHMAKER-1 #2076): WATCHMAKER_OPS time-gated-verification reads the consumer's own verification rows (cadence 2h) and probe-cadence reads the qnfo-cloud-ops scheduler_state stamp. 1.26.2 (2026-10-06, pillar cost): the ask-corpus-sync watchmaker entry says the feeder runs lean, not stopped, while an ai_spend cap is breached (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1). 1.26.1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy, OWNER-NO-LOOSE-ENDS-1): SAI-KAIZEN-GRADIENT-1 (#2054): computeSai kaizen = 1 / (1 + step x open issues), a gradient at every backlog size (the linear clamp read 0 above 20 open issues), in parity with qnfo-observability; WATCHMAKER-BY-PERSON-PRECISION-1 (#1726): code-task-merge counts a closed task as needing a person only when a person or session closed it or landed the change (23 of 53 counted rows were runner closures); WATCHMAKER_OPS gains owner-steps-watch (#2058, qnfo-cloud-ops) and dangling-bindings-census (#2051, qnfo-fleet-control). 1.26.0 UTM-CLICK-LEDGER-1 (transformation lever T7.9, pillar reach): the daily reach ingest reads qnfo-graph utm_clicks (written by qnfo-gateway 3.10.0 for every utm-tagged HTML page load, bot/human class, no cookie or IP) through the GRAPH binding into reach_signals source utm (channel = utm_source, entity campaign = utm_campaign, metric clicks_human / clicks_bot), so a social post or digest joins to the visits it caused; before the first tagged load the missing table is a note, not an error. 1.25.0 1.25.0 FLEET-CHANGELOG-1 (owner request 2026-10-06, pillar autonomy): a Changelog tab (/changelog, JSON /api/changelog, open to everyone) of what the fleet ships for itself: each worker version whose major or minor number is above every earlier one, and each worker Cloudflare created after 2026-09-29, from the canonical deploy ledger deployment_history; described from the commit on main that set the version (no model call), tagged with charter pillar and the public hostnames it serves, filterable (autonomy, public-facing, new workers, major, pillar); patch fixes are counted, not listed; an autonomy trend strip reads metric_history (watchmaker_index, metrics_in_breach, code_task_success_rate_30d, session_execution_ratio_30d); personal-plane releases in full only for the signed-in owner; synced in the existing 15-minute cron into qnfo-audit.fleet_changelog, heartbeat changelog-tick in WATCHMAKER_OPS. 1.24.1 (2026-10-06): WATCHMAKER_OPS ask-corpus-sync for qnfo-ai-search 2.2.8 ASK-CORPUS-FEEDER-1 (agent_issues 2029, carried for session 01KzS1 and PR 676); 1.24.1 is above PR 671's 1.24.0 (VERSION-AHEAD-1). 1.24.0 ATTENTION-LOOP-1 (2026-10-06, pillar reach; owner directive 2026-10-06 07:44Z: granular human attention per outreach channel and item, audit automatically, do more of what gets noticed, promote better or stop what is not): the reach ingest writes bot-filtered per-item rows (source cf-rum-human: pageviews per page, paper and referrer host; external_pageviews and continuation_pageviews per page) and the Buffer per-post metrics qnfo-cloud-ops collects (source buffer, per channel post); a daily scorecard after the ingest (attention_scorecard: items, human engagements, attention per item, referred visits, impressions per channel over 7 and 28 days; pages and papers noticed from outside; subscribers by source) with a verdict per social channel (INSUFFICIENT, STOP, PROMOTE, IMPROVE, KEEP, RETEST after 28 days) and a share in [0, 1] written to ops_config attention_channel_share, which qnfo-social multiplies into the owner caps and uses to order content by attention; every change is an attention_decisions row with evidence, a prediction and a 7-day verification that grades attention_decision_efficacy_30d; metrics attention_events_7d, attention_per_post_7d, pages_noticed_7d, attention_channels_stopped; GET /api/attention; WATCHMAKER_OPS attention-scorecard; no new cron, binding or model call. 1.23.2 (2026-10-06): the transformation-loop watchmaker entry names qnfo-fleet-control 0.4.132 (TP-1a parity, open-issue contract count, wave-exit stall); 1.23.1 (2026-10-06, pillar autonomy): WATCHMAKER_OPS measures TRANSFORMATION-LOOP-1 (qnfo-fleet-control 0.4.132: the transformation program engine, hourly; counted when i